.TH PLATMON-TRAY 1 "November 2026" "platmon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
platmon-tray \- show the state of a platmon service as a tray icon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B platmon-tray
.RI [ host[:port] ]
.br
.B platmon-tray
.RB [ --autostart " | " --no-autostart ]
.RI [ host[:port] ]
.br
.B platmon-tray
.RB [ --help " | " --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
platmon-tray shows the state of a running platmon service as an icon in the
desktop's tray: ok, warning, critical or not reachable, with the same levels
as the web page and the platmon command.
The default host is localhost and the default port is 9797.
.PP
The tooltip names the host and the state. When all is well it shows the CPU
and memory use and the hottest temperature; otherwise up to three readings
that need attention, critical ones first.
Not reachable means the service does not answer, or has no current data
(starting or stale).
Clicking the icon opens the web page in the default browser (xdg-open).
.PP
platmon-tray only reads the HTTP API: /api/status and /api/stats every
10 seconds and /api/observations every 60 seconds.
It never controls the service.
.PP
The icon is a StatusNotifierItem on the D-Bus session bus.
KDE Plasma, XFCE and Cinnamon show such icons as installed; Ubuntu's GNOME
shows them through its AppIndicator extension; other GNOME desktops need
that extension installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --autostart
Write
.I ~/.config/autostart/platmon-tray.desktop
so that the tray starts at the user's next login, with the host given, then
exit. The package starts nothing by itself.
.TP
.B --no-autostart
Remove that file, then exit.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A failure: no session bus, the session bus lost, or the autostart file not
written.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error.
.TP
.B 3
No StatusNotifierWatcher on the session bus: this desktop shows no tray
icons.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus (unix:path= or unix:abstract=); without it,
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the autostart file goes, instead of
.IR ~/.config .
.SH EXAMPLES
.B platmon-tray
.br
.B platmon-tray 192.168.1.10:9797
.br
.B platmon-tray --autostart
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR platmon (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
